[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Builder Pattern for Complex Object Construction and Immutability"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Builder design pattern is a creational pattern designed to solve the problem of telescoping constructors when creating objects with numerous optional parameters. It separates the construction of a complex object from its representation, allowing the same construction process to create various representations and enforcing thread-safe immutability upon completion."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The Telescoping Constructor Problem"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"When a class requires multiple configuration parameters—some mandatory and many optional—developers often resort to telescoping constructors. This anti-pattern involves creating multiple overloaded constructors taking an increasing number of parameters. As a result, code readability plummets, and maintenance becomes extremely error-prone."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"public class HttpRequest {
    private final String url;
    private final String method;
    private final int timeout;
    private final Map<String, String> headers;
    private final String body;

    // Telescoping constructors become unmanageable quickly
    public HttpRequest(String url) {
        this(url, "GET");
    }

    public HttpRequest(String url, String method) {
        this(url, method, 30000);
    }

    public HttpRequest(String url, String method, int timeout) {
        this(url, method, timeout, new HashMap<>());
    }

    public HttpRequest(String url, String method, int timeout, Map<String, String> headers) {
        this(url, method, timeout, headers, null);
    }

    public HttpRequest(String url, String method, int timeout, Map<String, String> headers, String body) {
        this.url = url;
        this.method = method;
        this.timeout = timeout;
        this.headers = headers;
        this.body = body;
    }
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing the Builder Pattern"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"To solve this, we extract the object creation process into a dedicated Builder class. The builder collects parameters step-by-step using fluent method chaining and finally constructs the immutable target object."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"public class HttpRequest {
    private final String url;
    private final String method;
    private final int timeout;
    private final Map<String, String> headers;
    private final String body;

    private HttpRequest(Builder builder) {
        this.url = builder.url;
        this.method = builder.method;
        this.timeout = builder.timeout;
        this.headers = Collections.unmodifiableMap(new HashMap<>(builder.headers));
        this.body = builder.body;
    }

    public static class Builder {
        // Required parameter
        private final String url;

        // Optional parameters initialized with default values
        private String method = "GET";
        private int timeout = 30000;
        private Map<String, String> headers = new HashMap<>();
        private String body = null;

        public Builder(String url) {
            this.url = url;
        }

        public Builder method(String method) {
            this.method = method;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder timeout(int timeout) {
            this.timeout = timeout;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder header(String key, String value) {
            this.headers.put(key, value);
            return this;
        }

        public Builder body(String body) {
            this.body = body;
            return this;
        }

        public HttpRequest build() {
            return new HttpRequest(this);
        }
    }
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Enforcing Immutability"},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"All fields in the target class are marked as final to guarantee they cannot be modified after construction."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"No setter methods are provided on the target class."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Mutable objects passed during construction (such as maps or collections) are deep-copied and wrapped using defensive constructs like Collections.unmodifiableMap to prevent external modification."},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Client Usage Example"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Using the builder results in highly readable, self-documenting code where the exact configuration parameters are explicitly named."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"HttpRequest request = new HttpRequest.Builder("https://api.example.com/data")
    .method("POST")
    .timeout(5000)
    .header("Authorization", "Bearer token123")
    .header("Content-Type", "application/json")
    .body("{"status":"active"}")
    .build();"}]
